      "problem": "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(-1,4).$",
